payload.description:
Every Papyrus feature epic ends with a docs page on the marketing and docs site, p.apyr.us (Papyrus-web).

Add a page covering automations as they ship:
- what an automation is (a trigger bound to a procedure);
- the trigger kinds (monitor today; schedule, event and manual coming);
- run history;
- the console Automation page;
- the papyrus automations CLI.

Use Distinctive Mark's TTAB rulings as the worked example. Update it as later slices land: review points, the Notification Center, story-state bots, the idea pipeline and cross-story checks. Source: docs/automations.md in Papyrus.

The Papyrus marketing website redesign session owns Papyrus-web. Coordinate with it before editing.

Acceptance: the page is live on p.apyr.us, linked from the docs index, and accurate to the released version.
